## 🔥 C++ Interview Roadmap (Most Asked → Least)

### 1️⃣ STL (MOST IMPORTANT – asked everywhere)

* vector

  * dynamic resizing, capacity vs size
  * push_back vs emplace_back
  * memory layout (contiguous)
* unordered_map / map

  * hashing vs RB tree
  * collisions, load factor
  * O(1) vs O(log N)
* set / unordered_set
* stack, queue, priority_queue (heap)
* deque, list (when & why)
* Algorithms

  * sort, binary_search
  * lower_bound / upper_bound
* Custom comparator (VERY IMPORTANT)

---

### 2️⃣ OOPs (CORE INTERVIEW AREA)

* Class, object, access specifiers
* Encapsulation, Abstraction
* Inheritance:

  * types (single, multiple, multilevel)
  * diamond problem
* Polymorphism:

  * compile-time (overloading)
  * runtime (virtual functions)
* Virtual function & vtable (VERY IMPORTANT)
* Constructor / Destructor order
* Object slicing

---

### 3️⃣ Memory Management (VERY VERY IMPORTANT)

* Stack vs Heap
* new/delete vs malloc/free
* Memory leak, dangling pointer
* Shallow vs Deep copy
* Rule of 3 / 5
* Copy constructor & assignment operator
* Placement new (basic idea)

---

### 4️⃣ Smart Pointers (HIGHLY ASKED)

* unique_ptr → exclusive ownership
* shared_ptr → reference counting
* weak_ptr → avoid cycles
* Circular dependency problem
* When to use what

---

### 5️⃣ Multithreading (IMPORTANT)

* thread creation
* mutex, lock_guard, unique_lock
* race condition
* deadlock
* condition_variable
* atomic operations

---

### 6️⃣ Modern C++ (C++11/14/17)

* auto, decltype
* range-based loops
* lambda functions
* move semantics (rvalue, std::move)
* perfect forwarding (basic idea)
* nullptr

---

### 7️⃣ Templates

* Function templates
* Class templates
* Template specialization
* Variadic templates (basic)

---

### 8️⃣ Exception Handling

* try, catch, throw
* stack unwinding
* RAII concept

---

### 9️⃣ Internal Working (DIFFERENTIATOR)

* How vector grows
* How unordered_map works internally
* map → Red-Black Tree
* vtable internals
* memory layout of object

---

## 📅 Study Plan

### Week 1

* STL (vector, map, set, heap)
* Practice STL-based questions

### Week 2

* OOPs (deep understanding)
* Memory Management

### Week 3

* Smart Pointers
* Modern C++ (lambda, move semantics)

### Week 4

* Multithreading
* Templates + Exception Handling

### Week 5 (Revision + Advanced)

* Internal working
* Mock interviews
* Revise weak topics

---

## ⚡ How to Study

* Understand concept
* Write small code examples
* Prepare interview answers (theory + code)

---

## 🎯 Must Focus (if short on time)

* STL + OOP + Memory + Smart Pointers

---

## 🧠 One-liner

Master STL + OOP + Memory → you clear most C++ interviews.
